<title>USA: Ticketmaster buys Canadian licensees.</title>
<headline>Ticketmaster buys Canadian licensees.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ticketmaster Group Inc. said Thursday it has agreed to buy its Canadian licensees, Vancouver Ticket Centre Ltd. and Ticketmaster Canada Inc., for a combination of cash and stock.</p>
<p>The price paid in the deal, which is expected to close by the end of next month, were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The Canadian licensees together sold about 7 million tickets last year.</p>
<p>Ticketmaster -- the leading U.S. provider of automated ticketing for concerts, plays, sports and other events -- sells 60 million tickets a year.</p>
<p>Ticketmaster said the acquisition was part of its strategy to consolidate its joint ventures and licensees to boost efficiency in its core ticketing business.</p>
</text>
